---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../lib/site.js";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Contact CurlToCode | Report a Bug or Request a Client"
  description="How to reach CurlToCode about a bug, an incorrect conversion, a client you would like supported, or a privacy question."
  eyebrow="Contact"
  heading="Contact"
  lede="One address, read by the person who builds the site."
  updated="2026-08-12"
  crumb="Contact"
  path="/contact"
>
  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p class="contact-address">
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    This is an independent project maintained by one person, so replies are not
    instant. Most messages get an answer within a few days.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting an incorrect conversion</h2>
  <p>
    This is the most useful kind of message we get, and the easiest to act on if
    you include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>the cURL command or code you pasted in;</li>
    <li>the language and client you selected;</li>
    <li>what the converter produced, and what you expected instead.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Please replace any real credentials before you send.</strong> A token
    is not needed to reproduce a bug — <code>Bearer redacted</code> works just as
    well, and we would rather not receive your secrets by email, since email is far
    less private than the converter itself.
  </p>

  <h2>Requesting a language or client</h2>
  <p>
    Tell us which client, and roughly what you are using it for. Targets are
    added where the client is mature or is the ecosystem standard, and where it
    is meaningfully different from something already supported.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy and legal</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about data handling go to the same address. Before writing, our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/cookies"
      >Cookie Policy</a
    > probably answer it — particularly the point that the converter never uploads
    what you paste. Requests concerning advertising data are usually for Google to
    answer rather than us, and we will say so and point you to the right place.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
